.TH velpic "" "Command"
.SH NAME
velpic \- a vellum drawing as troff pic source
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvelpic\fR \fIfile.d ...\fR > \fIfig.pic\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
velpic -- a vellum drawing as troff pic source
Usage:	velpic file.d ... > fig.pic
	The scale is PINNED at 16 grid units to the inch.
	The file name - is standard input.
.HE
.B velpic
writes the drawings named on its command line to standard output as
.B pic
source, for figures in manuals and reports.
Smooth polylines come out as pic splines; layers marked no-print, and
the construction layer, are skipped.
.PP
The scale is PINNED at 16 grid units to the inch and there is no
option to change it.
A figure that changed size when somebody passed a flag would set
differently in every document that included it, and the point of a
figure is that it does not.
.PP
The file name
.B \-
is standard input, so a generated drawing becomes a figure with no
temporary file:
.B "velinfo -symsheet pid.sym | velpic -" .
.SH EXAMPLES
A drawing per figure, in a Makefile:
.DS
.ta 8n
	.SUFFIXES: .d .pic
	.d.pic: ; velpic $< > $@
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B vellum ,
.B velplot ,
.B veldxf ,
.B nroff
.SH NOTES
A markup drawing from
.B "veldiff -mark"
is an ordinary drawing, so this program draws it: the review copy on
the wall and the figure in the manual come out of the same tool.
